speechtext:
Madam Speaker, under the provisions of Standing Order 43 I move, seconded by the hon. member for Winnipeg North Centre (Mr. Knowles):
That the Minister of Finance be instructed to make a statement on motions with respect to financial transactions between Mr. Roland Thornhill, minister of economic development for Nova Scotia, and a number of chartered banks in Nova Scotia and the retirement, resignation and transfer of a number of senior officers of those banks since those transactions occurred, and report to the House whether these transactions involved a breach of the Bank Act, the Criminal Code or financial ethics;
I further move that the Solicitor General consult with the attorney general of Nova Scotia with respect to the RCMP investigation which has been carried out and report to this House following these consultations.
